    "description": "Nava Toran Temple is located at Khor, Jawad census town, under Jawad tehsil in Neemuch district, Madhya Pradesh, India. It is an eleventh-century temple which consists of ten decorative arches arranged in two rows. The temple decorations include leaf-shaped borders, heads of makaras, and garland bearers, Nav or nou means \"nine\" and toran means \"pillars\"; this is where the temple gets its name. The prime deity of the temple is Varaha, who is the third avatar of lord Vishnu.",
